  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="5.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IVAtr">IV Atr</ref> 5.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="5.2" corresp="#wit-q">Et si aliquis eorum accusetur, sit Anglicus sit transmarinus, ladiet se pleno ordalio.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="la" source="#robertson" n="5.2" corresp="#wit-q">Et si aliquis eorum accusetur, sit Anglicus sit transmarinus, ladiet se pleno ordalio.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Und wenn einer von diesen [dreien] angeklagt wird, sei es ein Engländer, sei es ein Überseeischer, reinige er sich durch volles Ordal.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And if one of these [three] is accused, whether an Englishman or a man from overseas, let him clear himself by the full ordeal.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-q">And if one of them is accused, whether he be an Englishman or a foreigner, he shall clear himself by the full ordeal.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="235"><ref target="clause:IIAs_14-1">II As 14.1</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. II As. 14, 1</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:IVAtr_7-1">IV Atr 7.1</ref>; <ref target="clause:IVAtr_7-3">IV Atr 7.3</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares II As 14.1.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
